  "Nana (canción de cuna, mecida en 3/4)": "Lullaby (cradle song, rocked in 3/4)",
  "Nana de la luna": "Moon Lullaby",
  "Nana de la luna (Nana (canción de cuna, mecida en 3/4))": "Moon Lullaby (Lullaby (cradle song, rocked in 3/4))",
  "Negra (1) + puntillo (½) = pulso y medio. Casi siempre la sigue una CORCHEA que completa el segundo pulso: «taaa-i ta», un paso largo y uno corto. Cuenta «UN-o, DOS-y»: la negra con puntillo suena en el 1 y sigue sonando en el 2; la corchea entra en la «y» del 2. Es lo mismo que una negra ligada a una corchea.": "Quarter note (1) + dot (½) = one and a half beats. It is almost always followed by an EIGHTH NOTE that completes the second beat: “taaa-i ta”, one long step and one short step. Count “ONE-o, TWO-and”: the dotted quarter note sounds on 1 and keeps sounding on 2; the eighth note comes in on the “and” of 2. It is the same as a quarter note tied to an eighth note.",
  "Negra (2 corcheas) + puntillo (1 corchea) = 3.": "Quarter note (2 eighth notes) + dot (1 eighth note) = 3.",
  "Negra (4 semicorcheas) + puntillo (2) = 6.": "Quarter note (4 sixteenth notes) + dot (2) = 6.",
  "Negra + corchea + negra = 5 corcheas; faltaría una.": "Quarter note + eighth note + quarter note = 5 eighth notes; one would be missing.",
  "Negra con puntillo + corchea con manos alternas (D… I); en el xilófono, la nana completa.": "Dotted quarter note + eighth note with alternating hands (R… L); on the xylophone, the whole lullaby.",
  "Negra con puntillo con arco largo y la corchea con arco corto en el mismo sentido del arco siguiente; blanca con puntillo a arco entero, repartiendo el arco en tres pulsos.": "Dotted quarter note with a long bow and the eighth note with a short bow in the same direction as the next bow; dotted half note with the whole bow, dividing the bow over three beats.",
  "Negra con puntillo y corchea": "Dotted quarter note and eighth note",
  "Negra con puntillo, corchea, negra": "Dotted quarter note, eighth note, quarter note",
  "Negra, silencio de corchea y corchea: la llamada respira.": "Quarter note, eighth-note rest and eighth note: the call breathes.",
  "Negra-corchea con arco abajo largo y arco arriba corto (el «columpio» del arco); «La barquita» en las cuerdas del curso.": "Quarter note–eighth note with a long down bow and a short up bow (the “swing” of the bow); “The Little Boat” on the course strings.",
  "Neue Mozart-Ausgabe, serie IV/12 (consulta pública en dme.mozarteum.at) e IMSLP «Eine kleine Nachtmusik, K. 525»: violín 1, compases 1-4.": "Neue Mozart-Ausgabe, series IV/12 (public access at dme.mozarteum.at) and IMSLP “Eine kleine Nachtmusik, K. 525”: violin 1, bars 1-4.",
  "Nikolái Rimski-Kórsakov": "Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov",
  "Nikolái Rimski-Kórsakov fue oficial de la Marina rusa antes de dedicarse por completo a la música; de joven dio la vuelta a medio mundo en barco.": "Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov was a Russian Navy officer before devoting himself entirely to music; as a young man he sailed halfway around the world.",
  "Nikolái Rimski-Kórsakov — «El vuelo del moscardón», de la ópera «El cuento del zar Saltán» (1899–1900)": "Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov — “Flight of the Bumblebee”, from the opera “The Tale of Tsar Saltan” (1899–1900)",
