  "Un INTERVALO es la distancia entre dos notas. Se mide contando TODAS las notas, desde la primera hasta la segunda, las dos incluidas: do-mi = do, re, mi = 3 notas → TERCERA (3.ª). Do-sol = 5 → QUINTA (5.ª). Do-do agudo = 8 → OCTAVA (8.ª). La nota repetida (do-do) no es un salto: se llama unísono.": "An INTERVAL is the distance between two notes. It is measured by counting ALL the notes, from the first to the second, both included: C-E = C, D, E = 3 notes → THIRD (3rd). C-G = 5 → FIFTH (5th). C-high C = 8 → OCTAVE (8th). A repeated note (C-C) is not a leap: it is called a unison.",
